WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:15.334
"Caswell!" Josh yelled.

2
00:00:15.335 --> 00:00:18.666
"Where are you?" said Molly.

3
00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:22.386
"He's got to be here somewhere," said Mrs. O'Donnell.

4
00:00:22.387 --> 00:00:25.664
Everyone was still calling for Caswell.

5
00:00:25.665 --> 00:00:30.356
All at once we heard a small, muffled voice.

6
00:00:30.357 --> 00:00:36.075
"Here I am!" Caswell appeared from a dark space under the stairs.

7
00:00:36.076 --> 00:00:39.470
He was completely covered with dust.

8
00:00:39.471 --> 00:00:43.493
"Ah-choo!" Molly sneezed a few times.

9
00:00:43.494 --> 00:00:47.738
"Look what I found under the stairs!" said Caswell.

10
00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:51.105
He was clutching an old penny.

11
00:00:51.106 --> 00:00:55.352
"Caswell, I am so glad to see you," cried Mrs. O'Donnell.

12
00:00:55.353 --> 00:00:58.612
"When we couldn't find you, we were all very worried!"

13
00:00:58.613 --> 00:01:00.300
"I found a treasure!"

14
00:01:00.301 --> 00:01:04.042
said Caswell, proudly holding out his penny.

15
00:01:04.043 --> 00:01:05.755
"You are my treasure!"

16
00:01:05.756 --> 00:01:09.072
said Mrs. O'Donnell, hugging Caswell.

17
00:01:09.073 --> 00:01:13.886
"He's a pest, that's what he is," said Molly.

18
00:01:13.887 --> 00:01:17.768
But she was smiling as she ruffled her brother's hair.

19
00:01:17.769 --> 00:01:20.676
"I'm glad we found you."

20
00:01:20.677 --> 00:01:25.771
I couldn't wait to get back to my room to plan my new invention.

21
00:01:25.772 --> 00:01:28.287
It was going to be great.

22
00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:33.158
Caswell would never be lost again—at least not for long.

23
00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.810
The first thing I needed was a bell.

24
00:01:35.811 --> 00:01:40.664
Luckily, I knew just where to find one.

25
00:01:40.665 --> 00:01:46.129
My mom keeps a box of Christmas tree ornaments in our coat closet.

26
00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:50.190
One of the ornaments was a beautiful brass bell.

27
00:01:50.191 --> 00:01:53.415
I went in the closet and opened the box.

28
00:01:53.416 --> 00:02:00.303
I found lots of ornaments, including a colored glass ball and a gingerbread house.

29
00:02:00.304 --> 00:02:04.766
At last I found the brass bell.

30
00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:07.309
After that I got some string.

31
00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:10.501
I tied the bell to the string and jingled it.

32
00:02:10.502 --> 00:02:13.904
It made a nice loud ringing noise.

33
00:02:13.905 --> 00:02:19.232
If we could get Caswell to wear the bell, he'd jingle wherever he went.

34
00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:23.168
So we'd always be able to find him!

35
00:02:23.169 --> 00:02:29.050
I decided to bring the bell to school tomorrow to show Molly and the other kids.

36
00:02:29.051 --> 00:02:33.432
Then they would see that I was a really good inventor.

37
00:02:33.433 --> 00:02:36.891
By this time I was getting really hungry.

38
00:02:36.892 --> 00:02:41.134
I went into the kitchen to see what Mom was making for dinner.

39
00:02:41.135 --> 00:02:45.144
But Mom was still talking on the phone!

40
00:02:45.145 --> 00:02:48.392
There was nothing cooking on the stove.

41
00:02:48.393 --> 00:02:52.086
And there were no good smells coming from the oven.

42
00:02:52.087 --> 00:02:55.517
"What's the matter with Mom lately?" I wondered.

43
00:02:55.518 --> 00:02:58.969
"All she does is talk on the phone."

44
00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:05.047
And tonight it looked like she had forgotten to make dinner for Tate and me.

45
00:03:05.048 --> 00:03:10.620
I was about to look for something to eat when I heard something strange.

46
00:03:10.621 --> 00:03:15.012
"I'll have to rob a bank," my mom said into the phone.

47
00:03:15.013 --> 00:03:18.626
And then she laughed!

48
00:03:18.627 --> 00:03:19.964
Oh my gosh!

49
00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:22.729
My mom works as a bank teller.

50
00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:27.660
But that wouldn't turn her into a bank robber, would it?

51
00:03:27.661 --> 00:03:32.044
I decided I'd better tell someone about it right away.

52
00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:36.000
So I ran to Molly's apartment and knocked on the door.

53
00:03:36.001 --> 00:03:41.889
When Molly answered, I could smell something really good coming from her kitchen.

54
00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:47.646
It smelled like roast beef, which is my favorite food.

55
00:03:47.647 --> 00:03:52.259
"Molly, my mom is planning to rob a bank!" I cried.

56
00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:55.880
"What?" Molly blinked in surprise.

57
00:03:55.881 --> 00:03:59.291
"What on earth are you talking about, Iggy?"

58
00:03:59.292 --> 00:04:02.426
"I heard her on the telephone," I explained.

59
00:04:02.427 --> 00:04:04.824
"She said she was going to rob a bank.

60
00:04:04.825 --> 00:04:07.647
She even laughed about it!"

61
00:04:07.648 --> 00:04:09.738
Molly stared at me.

62
00:04:09.739 --> 00:04:12.409
"You know what?" she said.

63
00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:15.477
"What?" I said.

64
00:04:15.478 --> 00:04:20.198
I was hoping Molly would know how to stop my mother from robbing a bank.

65
00:04:20.199 --> 00:04:22.693
Molly shook her head.

66
00:04:22.694 --> 00:04:25.019
"You like to invent things, Iggy.

67
00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:31.176
And now you're inventing stories!"
